From 495156de4f8d81b7403993615804fccaf9527813 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:10:42 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] wayland: Tell a surface that follows its depth the
 person's element limit

The person's element limit (kwinrc [StereoDepth] ElementLimit, 1 pixel of a
view 1920 wide by default) is how far an element drawn inside a window may
lie in front of or behind the surface it lies on: one step of depth inside a
window. Stereo Union read it from kwinrc itself and nothing else had it, so
a toolkit drawing a window's elements at their own depth had no one place to
take its step from. KWin now has it as an option and tells it, with version
7 of kde_stereo_content_v1, to every kde_stereo_depth_v1 object: the event
element_limit, before output_width and depth_limits, again when it changes.

The limit is given as the person set it: no display factor is applied to it,
since none is designed for the elements inside a window (the sunk and popped
limits keep theirs). Resources of older versions hear nothing new.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
